Here is the exact step-by-step guide to configure Sign in with Solana (SIWS), Attack Protection, and Rate Limits in your Supabase Dashboard:
Step 1: Enable the Solana Web3 Provider
Open your Supabase Dashboard (aacrqdrcrfasfxcmtnjr).
In the left sidebar, go to Authentication → Sign In / Providers.
Scroll down to Web3 Wallet (or Solana) and click it.
Toggle Enable Sign in with Solana to ON.
Click Save.
Step 2: Whitelist Your SIWS Domain & URI (Required for EIP-4361 Validation)
Supabase validates every SIWS (EIP-4361) message by checking that the message's domain and URI match your allowed URLs. If they don't match, Supabase rejects the sign-in with an invalid URI/domain error.
Go to Authentication → URL Configuration.
Set Site URL to:
Text
https://actake.app
Under Redirect URLs, click Add URL and add:
Text
https://actake.app/**
Click Save.
(Actake's SIWS message uses actake.app and https://actake.app, so adding those ensures Supabase accepts the signed payload.)
Step 3: Set Up Attack Protection
Because anyone can generate unlimited Solana keypairs offline and call your Web3 sign-in endpoint, Supabase warns you to turn on abuse protection:
Go to Authentication → Attack Protection (in some dashboard views, Authentication → Bot and Abuse Protection).
